  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Good Emergency Management Practices Development (Phase 2) - Ecuador Poultry Industry</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This is the second of two workshops on avian influenza. During the first workshop, Ecuador&apos;s animal health officials identified several gaps in their development of Good Emergency Management Practices (GEMP) in regards to Avian Influenza via a table top simulation with the Latin American Poultry Association and the World Organisation for Animal Health. This follow-up project will support continued development of surveillance for poultry diseases and emergency and contingency plans for poultry disease outbreaks as well as assist Ecuador&apos;s effort to be recognized as free of avian influenza.</narrative>
  </description>
